Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: READ_ONCE NULL guard on the TTM *populate* path

Completes the protection from patch 18 on the other half of the TTM lifecycle:
amdgpu_ttm_tt_populate() dereferences ttm->pages[i]->mapping without checking
for NULL. A BO whose page array has holes (partial population after an aborted
GPU command) then dies with a kernel panic instead of an error. Guard each
entry with READ_ONCE + return -ENOMEM.

This is the exact form deployed in the build2 tree on blade 15
(snapshot snap-8fe794e8), verified by diff against the running module's
source tree.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
@@ -1223,8 +1223,12 @@ static int amdgpu_ttm_tt_populate(struct ttm_device *bdev,
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < ttm->num_pages; ++i)
-		ttm->pages[i]->mapping = bdev->dev_mapping;
+	for (i = 0; i < ttm->num_pages; ++i) {
+		struct page *p = READ_ONCE(ttm->pages[i]);
+		if (unlikely(!p))
+			return -ENOMEM;
+		p->mapping = bdev->dev_mapping;
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
